>>SOURCE FORMAT FREE

IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. ORE-BATCH.

ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT ORE-FILE ASSIGN TO "ore_batch.txt"
        ORGANIZATION IS LINE SEQUENTIAL.

DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD ORE-FILE.
01 ORE-RECORD PIC X(40).

WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 BATCH-ID PIC X(8) VALUE "BATCH001".
01 ORE-TONNES PIC X(7) VALUE "1000.00".
01 GOLD-GRADE PIC X(4) VALUE "2.50".
01 RECOVERY-RATE PIC X(5) VALUE "90.00".

PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    OPEN OUTPUT ORE-FILE

    MOVE SPACES TO ORE-RECORD

    STRING
        BATCH-ID DELIMITED BY SIZE
        " " DELIMITED BY SIZE
        ORE-TONNES DELIMITED BY SIZE
        " " DELIMITED BY SIZE
        GOLD-GRADE DELIMITED BY SIZE
        " " DELIMITED BY SIZE
        RECOVERY-RATE DELIMITED BY SIZE
        INTO ORE-RECORD
    END-STRING

    WRITE ORE-RECORD
    CLOSE ORE-FILE

    DISPLAY "COBOL ORE BATCH CREATED"
    DISPLAY "BATCH: BATCH001"
    DISPLAY "ORE TONNES: 1000.00"
    DISPLAY "GOLD GRADE: 2.50 G/T"
    DISPLAY "TARGET RECOVERY: 90.00%"

    STOP RUN.
